Another small update this week; the major change isn't even in the code
itself, actually.  However, this also serves to warn everyone; i'm going
to break save compatibility on the 9th (next Sunday).  If you have a
game running on the server, it would probably be a good idea to go ahead
and try to finish it.  :)

The change?  Precompiled Windows binaries will now be available from
http://sporkhack.nineball.org.  I'm not necessarily going to compile
this with every change I make, but I will update them each Sunday
as I post these announcements.  These binaries were compiled with MinGW,
so if you're trying to compile with that platform and having trouble,
let me know.  It will also compile under Visual C++ as well, if that's 
your preferred/available compiler.  The currently available version has 
all the changes in, including the most recent.

Speaking of:

9/1:
* When you finish your quest and report to your Quest Leader, your Quest 
  artifact will be made erodeproof
* Panic teleport now occurs _after_ trying to crawl out of water, not before
* Binary will now look for .sporkrc, defaults.sh (on win32/dos only), or 
  SporkHack.cnf; if it finds none of these, will drop through to old .nethackrc
  or other platform-specific config file
* Bug fix: stethoscopes will correctly detect non-critter eggs (currently 
  incorrectly detecting them)
* Bug fix: Don't show 'glows brown' if player is blind during destroy armor
* You-knew-this-was-coming fix: Backstab bonus on thrown weaponry removed
* High score list for nineball.org now available on webpage

This is worth reiterating: defaults.sh will _only_ be checked for on
win32/DOS platforms, not *nix... for what should be obvious reasons.

